=base:summary.cmark

A layout for technical documentation: the list of the pages, a search box, a
table of contents of the page, and links to the previous and next pages.

=base:main-content.cmark

Set the layout of a page to `documentation` to render it as a page of a
documentation. This very page is written with it: one sidebar lists the pages
of the documentation, the other one lists the headings of the page (on a narrow
screen both move above the content), the header has a search box, and the links
at the bottom lead to the previous and next pages of the documentation.

# Using the layout

In the `base:build-info.json` section of a page, use the `documentation`
layout and, optionally, a `group` and an `order`:

    =base:build-info.json
    {"layout":"documentation"
    ,"publicationStatus":"Public"
    ,"group":"The documentation layout"
    ,"order":30
    }

Then import the stylesheet of the layout next to the other ones, in a
`base:main-css.css` section:

    @import "/css/documentation.css";

You can also start such a page with
`kitchen-sink newarticle --layout documentation`.

# The table of contents

The table of contents lists the second and third level headings (`#` and `##`
in the markdown of the `main-content` sections). A page without any heading has
no table of contents.

# Moving between pages

All the pages that use the `documentation` layout are part of one
documentation, sorted as explained in [ordering documentation
pages](/documentation-ordering.html). Each page lists them all, see [navigation
and search](/documentation-navigation.html).
